From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Subject: net: increase skb pad for network optimizations

Increase the SKB padding to improve performance on embedded
devices with hardware offloading capabilities.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 include/linux/skbuff.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/include/linux/skbuff.h
+++ b/include/linux/skbuff.h
@@ -2875,7 +2875,7 @@ static inline int pskb_network_may_pull(
  * NET_IP_ALIGN(2) + ethernet_header(14) + IP_header(20/40) + ports(8)
  */
 #ifndef NET_SKB_PAD
-#define NET_SKB_PAD	max(32, L1_CACHE_BYTES)
+#define NET_SKB_PAD	max(64, L1_CACHE_BYTES)
 #endif
 
 int ___pskb_trim(struct sk_buff *skb, unsigned int len);
